  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **positive** integer `n`.\n\nOutput the integer obtained by removing all zeros from the decimal representation of `n`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** n = 1020030\n\n**Output:** 123\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nAfter removing all zeros from 1**0**2**00**3**0**, we get 123.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** n = 1\n\n**Output:** 1\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n1 has no zero in its decimal representation. Therefore, the answer is 1.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 1015`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
